  <Option name="designerParameterValues" />
  <Option name="groupBoxes" />
  <Option name="help" type="Map">
    <Option name="ALG_DESC" type="QString" value="Deterministic hillshade classification: elevation raster -&amp;gt; hillshade (fixed sun) -&amp;gt; block average onto a coarse grid -&amp;gt; 3 threshold classes -&amp;gt; sieve -&amp;gt; polygons -&amp;gt; smooth boundaries. Every step is a native QGIS or GDAL provider algorithm with explicit parameters; no randomness, no external scripts. The resample is the step that decides the look: thresholding the source raster directly yields over 127000 regions, 127000 of them under a hundredth of a square kilometre, because the class boundary is a per-pixel staircase. Averaging first yields a few hundred large regions and leaves the total area unchanged. Class 1 is below SHADOW_MAX, class 2 is SHADOW_MAX up to MID_MAX, class 3 is MID_MAX and above. NoData never becomes a class. Set SIEVE_PIXELS to 0 to keep every region. Polygon boundaries then follow coarse cell edges, so the last three steps round them off: Chaikin smoothing over many passes at a small offset, then vertex reduction at a tolerance well under a coarse cell, then a geometry repair. Smoothing moves each boundary by a small fraction of a cell, so the classes still sit on the same threshold." />
  </Option>
  <Option name="internal_version" type="QString" value="Version2" />
  <Option name="modelVariables" />
  <Option name="model_group" type="QString" value="Terrain" />
  <Option name="model_name" type="QString" value="hillshade_classes" />
  <Option name="outputGroup" type="QString" value="" />
  <Option name="outputOrder" />
